From cdd8c9690f8450a1c25b2b2b9cf2a0f48cf1f324 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 00:06:20 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] [SDL3-DOS] dos: patch 0142 -- GetDeviceBuf abandons the
 iteration when the SB ring has no room for a chunk

WHY DOS NEEDS THIS: DOSSOUNDBLASTER_PlayDevice copies a chunk into the
ISR ring with no room check of its own (patch 0141 counts the result),
and two writers reach it:
  - SDL_DOSAudioPump() (patch 0067) calls SDL_PlaybackAudioThreadIterate()
    directly, with no WaitDevice at all, and looks at room only
    afterwards, for its return value.
  - The background thread's while (Iterate()) WaitDevice() loop does check
    room, but in WaitDevice, which runs WITHOUT device->lock and, on the
    room-available path, calls DOS_Yield() (patch 0086, on by default)
    before returning. The main thread can pump into that last free chunk
    during the yield, and the thread's Iterate then writes into a full
    ring.
Either way the write lands on the chunk the IRQ handler plays next.

Evidence (dosags, PLAN.md step 8, 2026-09-22; all DOSBox-X, none yet on
real hardware):
  - SB live (no -silent, SB detection on), 5 Days a Stranger in play, OPL3
    music + SB PCM SFX, counter from 0141: before, overwrites=38 and 19,
    peak fill 1625 and 1578 ms against a 743 ms ring (cells OVW1, OVW3).
  - A first version put the room check at the top of SDL_DOSAudioPump.
    It gave overwrites=0 on 5 Days (OVW2, OVW4), but AGS Quest (music is
    SB PCM) still showed overwrites=1, peak 789/743 = capacity plus one
    46 ms chunk, in every run -- the WaitDevice-yield path above. Those
    AGS Quest runs came from the screen-equality gate; the same gate,
    before any guard, read 1237-3350 overwrites per run and peak fill
    50-148 s. (Corrected 2026-09-23: this message first said the gate
    ran with DOSBox-X's SB switched off. It did not -- its freeze-capture
    runs are interactive, never -silent, and their manifests show
    pcm_irqs 193-249, so the SB was playing, with detection skipped.
    The fill sizes are real mixer-speed overrun of a draining ring.)
    The single residual write past a full ring is what located the
    second path.
    The check has to sit where both writers pass under the lock.
  - This version (cells SBL1-SBL4, SB live): overwrites=0 and
    ring_max_ms <= 743 in every run, including AGS Quest SB PCM music
    (SBL4, 743/743); the ring fills to exactly capacity and waits there.
    SFX are not silenced: sound 10 gives pcm_irqs=227 on this build (SBL1,
    SBL3), identical to the pump-side version (OVW4).
Hardware confirmation pending.

WHAT: at the top of DOSSOUNDBLASTER_GetDeviceBuf -- called by
SDL_PlaybackAudioThreadIterate with device->lock held, before the stream
pull and before PlayDevice -- if ring_size - (ring_write - isr_ring_read)
< chunk_size, set *buffer_size = 0 and return. SDL's core treats
buffer_size == 0 as "abandon this iteration, try again next time"
(SDL_audio.c, the WASAPI convention): no stream pull, no PlayDevice. The
mixed data stays in the bound stream until the ISR frees a chunk.
SDL_DOSAudioPump's own post-iterate room test is unchanged, so it still
returns false on a full ring and a caller's pump loop still exits.

This is NOT the SDL/0050 gate that 0054 (Shape A) removed from this same
function (see the comment above the new block). 0050 returned
buffer_size = 0 when no bound stream had data, which is exactly the
moment a pull is needed to make SDL3_mixer's MixerCallback produce SFX,
so SFX went silent for the whole session. This gate never looks at the
streams. It holds only while the ring is full -- at least
ring_size - chunk_size of audio already queued for the ISR -- and
releases as soon as the ISR drains one chunk (~46 ms at 11025 Hz). With
room, behaviour is unchanged.

Side effect worth knowing: a port that pumped into a full ring used to
see its PCM "finish" at mix speed; now playback is paced by the device,
so a script step that waits on a sound ends on wall-clock time. dosags
saw exactly that make a tick-for-tick A/B screen gate row
non-deterministic under DOSBox-X, and moved that row to sound-off.

Source: dosags patches/SDL/0191 (From b20db8f346f4), re-derived here
against the hub series (line offset only; no dosags-only patch touches
GetDeviceBuf, PlayDevice, WaitDevice or SDL_DOSAudioPump). Comment tags
renumbered 0191 -> 0142.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Nz9XeKeVG8Ab7dm8esJsMu
---
 src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c | 25 ++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c b/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
index a2e06d64f..9309470ee 100644
--- a/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
+++ b/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
@@ -3564,7 +3564,30 @@ static Uint8 *DOSSOUNDBLASTER_GetDeviceBuf(SDL_AudioDevice *device, int *buffer_
        in tree for documentation per `pressure_test_tidy_narratives.md`
        -- fixing-the-wrong-layer is a useful negative-result reference),
        SDL/0053 (BeginShutdown semantic preserved). */
-    (void)buffer_size; /* unchanged; ring writes happen in PlayDevice */
+    (void)buffer_size; /* unchanged unless the ring is full (0142, below) */
+
+    /* DOS-PORT patch 0142: no room in the ISR ring for one chunk -> abandon
+       this iteration before the mix pull (SDL_audio.c: buffer_size == 0 means
+       "try again next time"; the core skips the stream pull AND PlayDevice).
+       PlayDevice has no room check of its own, and this is the one point
+       both writers pass under device->lock: the background thread's Iterate
+       (whose WaitDevice room check runs unlocked and then yields) and
+       SDL_DOSAudioPump's Iterate (which has no WaitDevice at all). The mixed
+       data stays in the bound stream until the ISR frees a chunk.
+       NOT the SDL/0050 gate that Shape A removed (comment above): that one
+       gated on "no bound stream has data", which is exactly when a pull is
+       needed to make the mixer callback produce SFX, so SFX went silent.
+       This gates only on "the ring is full" -- there is always at least
+       ring_size - chunk_size of audio queued for the ISR -- and it releases
+       as soon as the ISR drains one chunk (~46 ms at 11025 Hz). The stream
+       being empty never holds it. */
+    {
+        struct SDL_PrivateAudioData *hidden = device->hidden;
+        if ((hidden->ring_size - (hidden->ring_write - isr_ring_read)) < hidden->chunk_size) {
+            *buffer_size = 0;
+            return hidden->staging_buffer;
+        }
+    }
 
     /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 11 patch 0064, SFX-stall instrumentation
        part C): open the per-invocation SDL-DOS audio-callback timing
